node_modules/
new_token.txt
*.log
# …except this one. posted.log is the campaign's memory: it is the only record
# of which posts have gone out, and the daily workflow commits it back after
# every publish. Caught by "*.log" it was never committed, so alreadyPosted()
# read an empty set on every run, the sequence restarted at d01 each morning,
# and "Record what went out" reported nothing to record because git ignores an
# ignored file. Do not remove this negation.
!posted.log
.env

# ─── Never publish these ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo has to be PUBLIC, because Instagram's Content Publishing API
# does not accept an upload — you give it a URL and Meta fetches the file.
# So everything committed here is world-readable, permanently, including
# anything you later delete but do not rewrite out of history.
#
# STATUS.md is an internal working log. As of 10 Aug 2026 it contained a
# personal mobile number and a personal email address, which is exactly the
# sort of thing that must not end up in a public repo. It has never been
# committed — keep it that way.
STATUS.md
START-HERE.md

# Build scratch.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

